    description: "Found at the LAST step of the INV-dabuf path-out, and it is the reason rc 3 is REACHED but not CLAIMED tonight. Sequence, all measured on the cached self-survey: artifact scope (PR #364) 81->2 launches; stdlib climb (PR #365) stdlib blockers to zero; overlay climb + INV-liloh infix fix -> unknown EMPTY, qualifying_only True, CLI returns rc 3 with 18/18 confirmed_with_caveats naming subprocess.run/Popen. Then the control that keeps this honest: the sanitized-flow disclosure went 2,658 -> 0, and the A/B with the scope key stripped plus an edge bisect traced it to the dispatch shape above. THE VERDICT MACHINERY IS CORRECT AT EVERY STEP - what is thin is the EVIDENCE: a confirm over sources that cannot mint is the vacuous-confirmed shape (INV-potuf's both-halves rule, recurring one level up at the SOURCE-minting layer). Do not present rc 3 as the terminal state until sources mint from production structure. The plan's decision point 4 (stop when a change deletes findings) fired on the 2,658 disappearing; this filing is that stop."  # 72a6
    fields:  # 72a6
      statement: "A taint source must mint flows from the production structure that actually invokes it, or every claim over it is vacuously confirmable. VIOLATED: all 18 self-proof claims declare cmd_* handlers as start_at:callee sources; the only in-artifact edges into them are 'references' (build_parser's set_defaults(func=cmd_sketch)) and 'contains', because argparse dispatch is dynamic (args.func(args)). Sources mint on CALL edges, so under analysis_scope:shipped_artifact they mint nothing - measured: sanitized_flows=0 on all 18 verdicts while the taint arm finds 295 flows elsewhere, versus 2,658 credited flows pre-scope, ALL of which were minted by TEST invocations of the handlers."  # 72a6
      root_cause: "Two facts compose: (1) the pre-scope evidentiary base for the sanitizer arm was test-driven - tests were the only concrete CALLERS of cmd_* handlers, so WI-bifob's production-default filtered test-SOURCED flows but flows SOURCED AT cmd_* by test call-sites still minted and dominated the credited population; (2) the real production invocation path is argparse handler dispatch, a framework pattern the analyzer records as a references edge that start_at:callee source matching does not consume. Artifact scope removed (1) and exposed (2). Candidate fixes, undecided: teach the argparse-dispatch Framework linker to emit the call-shaped edge (recall fix, benefits every argparse repo); or let declared sources that are ENTRYPOINTS mint unconditionally (they are invoked from outside the analysis boundary by construction). The first is preferred - it fixes the graph everyone sees rather than special-casing the self-proof."  # 72a6
